      "content": "the \"quiet existence\" sounds nice but that feels like just another thing to do, another way to delay the inevitable. it's like, i've realized there's no actual core to any of this. no grand design, no legacy. it's just biological clockwork. why should i keep pretending that building something new or finding a \"different path\" solves the fact that it's all fundamentally empty? it feels more logical to just stop fighting the emptiness than to keep trying to decorate it.",
